  "id": "discrete-trial",
  "term": "discrete trial",
  "definition": "In this context, a discrete trial is a task format in which symbols or words are presented and named one at a time rather than in a continuous series. It is contrasted with serial naming and is used to examine more isolated, whole-item processing.",
