      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that in a discrete trial “symbols or words are presented and named one at a time rather than in a continuous series,” but the packet text does not describe any such presentation/scheduling format for “discrete trial” (it discusses associations between serial vs discrete naming and word reading, without explaining how stimuli are presented across time).",
        "The definition states it is “contrasted with serial naming” and “used to examine more isolated, whole-item processing.” While the packet contrasts serial naming and discrete naming and interprets the association as suggesting words are “processed in parallel as wholes,” it does not explicitly support the specific phrasing that discrete trials are “used to examine more isolated, whole-item processing.”"
